Now I need to implement the suffix automaton. The structure requires states with transitions, suffix links, and length tracking. I'll initialize with a root state, then process each character by creating new states and managing the suffix links appropriately.

When extending with character c, I create a new state cur with length one more than the previous state. I follow suffix links from the last state, adding transitions to cur until I find a state p that already has a transition on c or reach the root. If no such transition exists, I link cur to the root. Otherwise, I check if the existing transition leads to a state with the expected length—if so, I use it as cur's link. If not, I need to clone that state to maintain the automaton's properties.

For the clone, I copy q's transitions and suffix link, set its length to p's length plus one, then redirect both q and cur to point to the clone. I also update all of p's suffix chain transitions that pointed to q to now point to the clone. Finally, I update last to cur.

